{"title":"Career Roadmap · Glass Artist","role":"Glass Artist","summary":"A Glass Artist creates functional, decorative, sculptural, architectural, and conceptual works using glass as the primary medium. A B.Des in Ceramic & Glass Design provides a strong foundation in glass forming, kiln work, hot/cold techniques, material experimentation, design thinking, craft practice, studio production, and contemporary art.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Des (Bachelor of Design)","Course":"Ceramic & Glass Design"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"flow","items":["The strongest professional profile combines material mastery","artistic identity","design skills","studio practice","portfolio","business knowledge."],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Area","Details"],"rows":[[{"text":"Degree"},{"text":"B.Des – Ceramic & Glass Design"}],[{"text":"Primary Career"},{"text":"Glass Artist"}],[{"text":"Core Material"},{"text":"Glass"}],[{"text":"Major Techniques"},{"text":"Hot glass, kiln forming, fusing, slumping, casting, coldworking"}],[{"text":"Supporting Skills"},{"text":"Drawing, sculpture, material research, installation"}],[{"text":"Tools"},{"text":"Kiln, furnace, torches, grinders, polishing equipment, moulds"}],[{"text":"Digital Skills"},{"text":"CAD, 3D modelling, digital fabrication"}],[{"text":"Workplaces"},{"text":"Studios, galleries, design companies, craft organisations, museums"}],[{"text":"Alternative Careers"},{"text":"Glass Designer, Product Designer, Studio Artist, Art Educator"}],[{"text":"Key Differentiator"},{"text":"Distinctive material language + technically strong portfolio"}]]}]},{"heading":"What Does a Glass Artist Do?","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A professional Glass Artist may create:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sculptures"},{"text":"Vessels"},{"text":"Decorative objects"},{"text":"Lighting products"},{"text":"Architectural installations"},{"text":"Public art"},{"text":"Jewellery"},{"text":"Tableware"},{"text":"Art glass"},{"text":"Experimental glass forms"},{"text":"Mixed-media installations"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The work can range from traditional craftsmanship to contemporary conceptual art."},{"type":"p","text":"A professional workflow may look like:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Idea","Research","Sketches","Material Experimentation","Prototype","Glass Formation","Coldworking / Finishing","Testing","Final Artwork","Exhibition / Commission / Sale"]}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Experience","Possible Position"],"rows":[[{"text":"0–2 years"},{"text":"Studio Assistant"}],[{"text":"1–3 years"},{"text":"Junior Glass Artist"}],[{"text":"2–5 years"},{"text":"Glass Artist / Glass Designer"}],[{"text":"4–7 years"},{"text":"Independent Studio Artist"}],[{"text":"5–10 years"},{"text":"Senior Glass Artist"}],[{"text":"7–12 years"},{"text":"Studio Lead / Workshop Head"}],[{"text":"8–15 years"},{"text":"Art Director / Glass Design Consultant"}],[{"text":"10+ years"},{"text":"Established Artist / Studio Founder"}],[{"text":"Long-term"},{"text":"International Artist / Educator / Curator"}]]}]},{"heading":"Year 1 — Design & Material Foundations","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The first year should establish fundamental design and studio skills."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Drawing"},{"text":"Perspective"},{"text":"Composition"},{"text":"Colour theory"},{"text":"Form studies"},{"text":"Design fundamentals"},{"text":"Sculpture basics"},{"text":"Material exploration"},{"text":"Visual research"},{"text":"Art history"},{"text":"Craft traditions"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Material experiments"},{"type":"p","text":"Explore:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Transparency"},{"text":"Opacity"},{"text":"Colour"},{"text":"Light transmission"},{"text":"Reflection"},{"text":"Texture"},{"text":"Su